        <title>Explorer</title>
        <item>
            <title>1.6.1</title>
            <pubDate>Wed, 04 Nov 2026 14:39:48 +0900</pubDate>
            <sparkle:version>54</sparkle:version>
            <sparkle:shortVersionString>1.6.1</sparkle:shortVersionString>
            <sparkle:minimumSystemVersion>14.0</sparkle:minimumSystemVersion>
            <description><![CDATA[<h3>Added</h3>
<ul>
<li><b>Korean:</b> Explorer now speaks Korean on a Mac set to Korean, using the same words as the Windows 11 File Explorer (숨긴 항목, 미리 보기 창, 속성…).</li>
<li>Toolbar buttons show their name and shortcut when you hover over them.</li>
<li>In Details and List views, <b>→</b> opens the selected folder and <b>←</b> goes up to the parent folder. Opening a folder from the keyboard (<b>→</b> or <b>Return</b>) selects its first item, so you can keep going with the arrows.</li>
<li><b>Tab</b> moves the focus folder tree → file list → search box and around again (<b>Shift-Tab</b> goes back). Tabbing into a list with nothing selected selects the first item, so you can see where you are; an empty folder is skipped.</li>
<li>Icon views show whether they have the keyboard focus: the selection is in the accent color while focused and grey otherwise, like the Details list.</li>
<li>Filter bar: a new <b>Other</b> kind button for files that aren't folders, images, documents, audio, video, or archives (apps, disk images, source code…), so turning on every kind button shows every item.</li>
</ul>
<h3>Changed</h3>
<ul>
<li>View menu: the Pro toggles (Item Check Boxes, Stash Shelf, Group by, Dual-Pane View) now sit together below the free ones.</li>
<li>The folder-tree option "Show All Folders" is now <b>Show Subfolders of</b> Opened Folder<b>, named for what it does; Settings explains both tree</b> options.</li>
<li>Home: the recent lists' button reads <b>Clear History</b>.</li>
<li>Pinned Desktop, Downloads and the other standard folders show the names macOS uses in your language.</li>
<li>Clearer wording in places: the license note, folder-access prompts, What's Using This (<b>Items in Use</b>, <b>Stop Using in Explorer</b>), and two-way sync (<b>Both (newer wins)</b>).</li>
</ul>
<h3>Fixed</h3>
<ul>
<li>At Macintosh HD, ←, Backspace or Go ▸ Enclosing Folder reloaded the drive and dropped the selection; they now do nothing there.</li>
</ul>
]]></description>
